2026-09-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2258) 'Run a `ci-*` hook locally with `GATE_BASE` set; the sections below hold what was measured.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2258) 'every CI gate is a prek hook
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2258) 'The workflow has one job, `prek`. Gates that need only the tree are ordinary hooks. Gates that need a base ref or a code-host token are `ci-*` hooks in the manual stage, which the job calls by id with `GATE_BASE` and `GH_TOKEN` set; a local commit never runs them. An unset `GATE_BASE` fails the hook. The merge queue requires no check (operator, 2026-11-13), so both steps of the job are run on the desk before a pull request is enqueued.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written

