2026-09-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2258) 'What is measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2258) 'Locally through prek 0.5.3, `ci-comment-ladder`, `ci-trope-density`, `ci-spdx` and `ci-rfd-canary` pass on `main/main`, and `ci-comment-ladder` fails with `GATE_BASE` unset. On the pull request that landed it, `prek` passed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2258) 'Warnings kept honest
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2258) 'jose 1.11.12, pulled in by ex_mcp, uses bare `catch`, which OTP 29 deprecates. The job silences that one warning only when jose, OTP and Elixir read 1.11.12, 29 and 1.20.4, and any other tuple leaves the warnings on with a notice naming what it found.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2258) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2258) 'Nine jobs repeated checks prek could run, each rendering the RFDs again, and the ruleset required nine names that had to match the workflow by hand. The list the working agreements stated had already drifted from the ruleset.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2258  1 LINE
 Text:Written
